Placeholder that keeps frontend/dist non-empty.

main.go embeds the build output with //go:embed all:frontend/dist, and a Go
embed pattern that matches no files is a compile error. The build output itself
is not committed, so on a fresh clone `go build`, `go vet` and `go test` would
fail before anyone has run a frontend build.

Two things keep that from happening, and both are needed:
  - frontend/dist/.gitkeep is committed (see the negation in .gitignore), which
    covers the clone-before-first-build case;
  - this file lives in frontend/public, which Vite copies into dist on every
    build, restoring the placeholder that emptyOutDir had just deleted.
